<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabriel de Gabrieli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1671–1747</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabriel de Gabrieli was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> architect from Roveredo in the Italian-speaking part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a>. After serving as court architect at Ansbach, he became court architect to the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eichstatt">Eichstätt</a> in 1714 and designed many of the buildings that give the town its baroque character, including parts of the Residenz and noble town houses.</p></div>
